  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Trying to find a legal excuse to fire Denis despite Barinov's protection, Mikhail stages a surprise breathalyzer test in the kitchen and then arranges for cleaner Gulya to send Denis upstairs. Listen to the scene.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Сегодня плановая проверка на алкоголь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Слушай, выпей немного оливкового масла.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Оно всегда отлично помогает.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Теперь ты, давай дуй.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А что тут у вас происходит?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Это новое распоряжение начальства.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ну, если начальство нам приказало.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Михаил, покажите нам личный пример.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Дуйте сами в эту трубочку.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "А я сегодня уже дул.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Мне ещё весь отель проверять.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Никто не видел, где все тележки?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Денис, можешь мне помочь, пожалуйста?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Спасибо, вот у тебя карточка.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Сегодня плановая проверка на алкоголь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Today is a scheduled check for alcohol.' The meaning hinges on 'tonight' working together with 'alcohol' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Слушай, выпей немного оливкового масла.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Listen, drink a little olive oil.' In Russian, the idea of 'listen' flows naturally into 'butter' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Оно всегда отлично помогает.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It always helps wonderfully.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'it' and finishing on 'is helping'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Теперь ты, давай дуй.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Now you, go ahead and blow.' The meaning hinges on 'now' working together with 'blow' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А что тут у вас происходит?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And what is going on here with you?' The grammar packs 'and' and 'is happening' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange. Mikhail answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Это новое распоряжение начальства.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is a new order from management.' Mikhail brings out the contrast between 'this' and 'new' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ну, если начальство нам приказало.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well, if management ordered us.' Chef Barinov anchors the line on 'come on', while 'ordered' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Михаил, покажите нам личный пример.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Mikhail, show us a personal example.' The grammar packs 'Mikhail' and 'example' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Дуйте сами в эту трубочку.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Blow into this tube yourself.' The meaning hinges on 'blow' working together with 'breathalyzer tube' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "А я сегодня уже дул.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And I already blew today.' The grammar packs 'and' and 'blew' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Мне ещё весь отель проверять.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I still have to inspect the whole hotel.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'to me' and finishing on 'to check'. Gulya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Никто не видел, где все тележки?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Has anyone seen where all the carts are?' The '-l' ending on the verb meaning 'saw' places the action in the masculine past tense.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Денис, можешь мне помочь, пожалуйста?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Denis, can you help me, please?' The meaning hinges on 'Denis' working together with 'please' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Спасибо, вот у тебя карточка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Thank you, here is the key card for you.' In Russian, the idea of 'thank you' flows naturally into 'key card' without extra filler words. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
